# =============================================================================
# GOVERNANCE RULES AND GUIDELINES FOR AI AGENTS — TREEGOV
# Project: TreeGov — Risk Segmentation Workbench
# =============================================================================

## MANDATORY when starting or resuming a session

1. Read README.md in full.
2. Read docs/methodology.md, docs/audit_log.md, and the philosophy document (docs/philosophy.md in English, docs/philosophy.es.md in Spanish).
3. Read this file (.treegovrules) in full.

## White-box rules (HARD RESTRICTION)

1. FORBIDDEN to use: sklearn, scikit-learn, statsmodels, xgboost, lightgbm, catboost.
2. Only allowed: numpy, pandas, scipy.stats.
3. Every statistical formula must be written explicitly in the code, with its bibliographic citation in the docstring.

## Clean-room architecture

1. backend_v3/ MUST NOT import PySide6 or anything from frontend_v3/.
2. frontend_v3/ MUST NOT implement analytical logic.
3. SplitConfig is the common contract between engines. Its immutability (frozen dataclass) is sacred.

## MRM / IFRS 9 governance

1. Any PD calculation must include the Jeffreys estimator and the PD Floor.
2. Every model decision must be auditable: transactional DEBUG log per run.
3. Tests must include reference values verified by hand (not just self-references).

## Protected zones (NEVER touch without explicit authorization)

- .venv/
- data/
- archive/
- logs/ (write-access only via log_config.py)

## Mandatory documentation

1. Every architectural decision is recorded in docs/audit_log.md.
2. Every bug fix is recorded with its numerical trace.
3. Obsolete documents are moved to archive/legacy_docs/ with a historical header, never deleted.

## Language

- Code: English.
- Documentation: English (default).
- Bilingual documents: README and philosophy (both English and Spanish).
- Historical document: audit_log.md (kept in Spanish for traceability).
- File and module names: English.

## Anti-leakage

Any imputation (mean/mode) is computed EXCLUSIVELY on the training fold. TrainOnlyImputer is the only authorized channel.

## Prohibitions in public documentation

- Do not mention third-party trademarks nor the names of the predecessor project.
- Do mention: academic citations (Kass, Breiman, etc.), regulatory standards (Basel, IFRS 9, SR 11-7).

## Verification

Before modifying existing code: read README.md, docs/methodology.md and this file.
